{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"forcible-diminished-lamb","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context\n\nGeneric text search can miss Terraform declarations in sibling files or local child modules and can overstate computed expressions. This REB-640 child delivers the first useful end-to-end path: safe structural evidence for plan-review T10 Pass 1 and independent Pass 2. The parent plus `src/rebar/grounding/evidence.py` and `src/rebar/schemas/grounding.schema.json` are authoritative.\n\n## Scope\n\n### Optional boundary\n\n- Add `grounding-terraform = [\"python-hcl2==8.1.3\"]` to `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock`.\n- Register the `hcl2` probe in `_optional.py` and an ABSTAIN-posture `grounding_terraform` capability in `_capabilities.py`.\n- Extend optionality CI and lean-runtime tests. Core import, generic grounding, and non-Terraform reviews must not import `hcl2`.\n- Installing the extra is the sole opt-in; add no core config key.\n\n### Structural index\n\nAdd `terraform_index.py` and `terraform_tools.py` under `src/rebar/grounding/`. A per-agent-call session scans safely, reads eligible files into an immutable byte snapshot, then passes bytes—not host paths—to `python-hcl2` through `grounding.harness.run_in_worker`.\n\n- Terraform scope exists when file impact names `.tf` / `.tf.json`, or the plan names Terraform/OpenTofu and the repository contains Terraform files.\n- Treat every `.tf` and `.tf.json` sibling in an affected directory as one module. Recursively follow literal repo-contained local module sources and include literal in-repo reverse callers. Exclude VCS metadata, virtualenvs, and `.terraform/`.\n- Parse a changed `.tfvars` only when explicitly targeted; never apply it as selected module input.\n- Before emitting evidence, enforce 64 modules, 5,000 Terraform files, 32 MiB, and the existing 60-second timeout. Exceeding any bound yields one abstention and no partial facts.\n- Use parser locations for HCL. For Terraform JSON, return an exact line only for an unambiguous key occurrence; otherwise return file-level location.\n- Abstain when a query depends on duplicate addresses, invalid/unreadable files, out-of-repo sources, escaping symlinks, dynamic sources, splat/index-dependent traversals, computed values, or provider-defined attributes.\n\n### Operations and receipts\n\nExpose two plain agent tools:\n\n- `lookup_declaration(address, module_path=\"\")` locates variables, locals, outputs, modules, providers, managed resources, and data resources.\n- `resolve_reference(reference, from_file)` resolves direct module-scope traversals and a declared output of a repo-local child. It can confirm a resource declaration base but not a provider-defined attribute.\n\nUse existing positive `match` / absence-refuting `refuted` outcomes where applicable; anything unprovable is `abstain`. No result asserts nonexistence.\n\nReturn canonical JSON containing evidence, safe structural facts, and a receipt: normalized query, snapshot/module digest, backend and analyzer versions, effective limits, outcome, and result digest. Never return credential or string/number literal payloads; return type, safe classification such as wildcard/empty, digest, and span.\n\n### Plan-review integration\n\n- Inject both tools into Terraform-scoped T10 Pass-1 requests only.\n- A Terraform-scoped T10 finding selects agentic Pass 2. Inject a fresh session only into that verifier. Pass 2 must call a tool; it receives no implicit Pass-1 answer. Immutable parse bytes may be reused, but query ledgers are per call.\n- Extend `RunnerAgentStep` with a generic per-call extra-tool provider/finalizer while preserving existing static `extra_tools`.\n- Merge actual reads into `_usage.distinct_fetches` as synthetic `read_file` entries. Add validated `**/*.tf` and `**/*.tf.json` membership entries to the signed read set so a later sibling addition changes freshness without importing `hcl2` at claim time.\n- If the extra is absent, advertise no tools and leave review behavior unchanged. Once advertised, parse/path/limit failures return closed abstentions and never escape or become deterministic blockers.\n\n## Positive rationale\n\nThis vertical slice produces evidence in both review passes and pins what it read. It reuses Rebar's worker, evidence, tool-injection, usage, and glob-freshness seams; it adds neither a scanner stage nor Terraform evaluation.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nRegistry access, remote content, `terraform-config-inspect`, policy scanners, reviewer-prompt edits, and every Terraform/OpenTofu/provider executable. Later children add source probing and corroboration.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `nava-rebar[grounding-terraform]` installs exactly `python-hcl2==8.1.3`; capability and lean-core subprocess tests prove absence degrades to ABSTAIN and non-Terraform imports/reviews neither import `hcl2` nor advertise the tools.\n- [ ] Unit fixtures prove a changed file resolves declarations from sibling `.tf` / `.tf.json` files and bounded local child/reverse-call modules; an explicitly targeted `.tfvars` is reported but never selected as input.\n- [ ] Both operations return schema-valid canonical evidence/receipts for static declarations and local child outputs; computed/provider/dynamic/ambiguous cases return a closed abstention with no raw literal.\n- [ ] Containment, parse failure, timeout, and each 64-module/5,000-file/32-MiB boundary return one abstention with zero partial facts, and the worker is reaped.\n- [ ] A workflow integration test captures real T10 Pass-1 and agentic Pass-2 requests, observes both tools with distinct query sessions, and observes none for non-T10 or non-Terraform controls.\n- [ ] A signed-read-set contract test observes every parsed file and both membership patterns, then adds a sibling `.tf` and proves the stdlib-only freshness digest changes.\n- [ ] A subprocess spy records no launch of Terraform, OpenTofu, providers, tfparse, TFLint, Trivy, terraform-ls, or terraform-docs.\n\n## Testing\n\nTest contract card:\n\n- Authoritative contract: REB-640, `docs/grounding.md`, and `grounding.schema.json`.\n- Preconditions: a temp repo with sibling declarations, a local child output, a reverse caller, dynamic expressions, an escaping symlink, and limit fixtures.\n- Production path: real file capture → real worker parser → tool response; real plan-review request construction with only the model boundary faked.\n- Tiers: unit/contract for parsing and evidence; workflow integration for batch/agent/read-set routing; lean-install subprocess for import isolation.\n- Oracles: exact outcome/reason/location/receipt, exact tool names per request, zero partial facts, and changed membership digest after file creation.\n- Negative controls: CloudFormation-only T10 and Python plans have no tools; a direct literal reference resolves while the nearest computed form abstains.\n- CI: `make test` plus `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`.\n\n## Verification\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_index.py tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_tools.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py tests/unit/test_capabilities.py`","id":"08ab-60d2-3082-4b47","parent_id":"a374-849c-c8f2-4234","priority":2,"tags":["terraform","grounding","llm","optional","plan-review"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Plan-review Terraform structural grounding vertical slice"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788469424717431454,"uuid":"f5501e6f-84bd-468e-84af-b66469daf388"}